<!-- Hollowmere player preservation roots (P3.1; IL2CPP, managed stripping Low).

     Most of the game survives stripping because real code reaches it: the scenes and assets reference every
     MonoBehaviour/ScriptableObject type, the gameplay plugins are composed through direct generic registrations
     (ManagedSystemRegistration<TSystem>, recipe/factory delegates), and the checkpoint codecs are direct references.

     The one entry point no managed call site keeps alive is the generated world catalog:
     GameCore.Gameplay.World.GameplayCatalog.TryBuild resolves the catalog class by the full name the bake recorded in
     the region manifest (RegionManifest.CatalogTypeName, "Hollowmere.Generated.HollowmereCatalog") with
     Assembly.GetType and invokes its public static BuildCatalog() by reflection (GameplayBoot.cs), so gameplay code
     never references the generated assembly. Without this entry the linker removes the whole assembly and the player
     boots with "catalog type not found". The assembly is generated (World/Generated), so it is preserved whole.

     Newtonsoft.Json is only referenced by Editor-only Studio assemblies, so nothing is needed for it here. -->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="Hollowmere.World.Generated" preserve="all" />
  <!-- The application bootstrap is found by the Entities world initialization through reflection over the
       ICustomBootstrap implementations, never by a managed call site (A11: Hollowmere registers its definition with it). -->
  <assembly fullname="GameCore.Unity.Adapters">
    <type fullname="GameCore.Unity.Adapters.GameCoreApplicationBootstrap" preserve="all" />
  </assembly>
</linker>
